* Model of a simple surge arrestor (spark gap arrestor) = Überspannungsableiter mit Funkenstrecke
* Model of MOV = voltage dependent resistor = Überpannungsableiter (from the ltspice yahoo group)

* spark gap:

* http://www.spectrum-soft.com/news/winter99/sparkgap.shtm
* http://www.intusoft.com/nlhtm/nl50.htm#SPARKGAPMODELING

* This macromodel was derived based on an article by Christophe Basso titled "SPICE model simulates spark-gap arrestor" which appears in * the July 3, 1997 issue of EDN. This model does not simulate the glow transition of a spark-gap. There are seven parameters for this
* macro. The parameters are defined as follows:


* vthres = voltage at which the sparkgap strikes
* varc = voltage across the sparkgap once struck
* isus = Sustaining current under which th arc is stopped
* rneg = negative resistance once struck (I set it to 1 instead of -1 because energy have to be >0 not <0 !!!)
* lpl = lead inductance
* rpl = flux loss associated with lpl
* cpar = Gap inductance
* carc = Arc capacitance
* cthresh = switcher capacitance of R,C network for smoother on/off transition (convergence)
* ron = on resistance of switcher 
* roff = off resistance of switcher 

* set the parameter values above to your needs
* the parameters of the following models are only set
* with rudimentary values !!!!!!!!
* Especially the table source values have to be set to appropriate values 
* of the data sheet of your arrester

* NOTE: sparkgap models often laks of convergence !!!!!
* use MOV instead 

* resistance of surge arrester is not dependent of volt/us 
.SUBCKT SPARK 1 2 params: vthres=90 varc=10 isus=500m rneg=-1 lpl=130n rpl=2.5k cpar=1p carc=3p
+ tfall=10u trise=10u cthresh=0.1p ron=0.1 roff=1g ioff=100m
.param rparsw=1e12
VDUM1 1 10 0
LPL1 10 11 {lpl} rser=0
RPL1 10 11 {rpl}
CPAR1 1 2 {cpar}
RLEAK1 1 2 {rparsw}
RNEG1 11 17 {rneg}
DTRK1 12 17 DCLAMP
DSRK2 12 16 DCLAMP
CARC1 1 16 {carc}
* G-SWITCH
G1 16 2 VALUE={v(16,2)*v(13)}  tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
R5 16 2 {rparsw} 
* Changed to SW switch
*S1 16 2 13a 0 switch
*a1 13 0 0 0 0 0 13a 0 or trise={trise} tfall={tfall}
*.model switch SW (vt=0.5 vh=-0.4 ron=10 roff=1e9) 
* SWITCH END
* Switch control input
*BARC 15 0 v=if(ABS(V(1,2))>{vthres},10,if(ABS(I(VDUM1))>{isus},10,{goff})) tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
BARC 15 0 v=if((ABS(V(1,2))>{vthres}),{1/ron},if(((DDT(ABS(I(VDUM1)))>0 & ABS(I(VDUM1))>ioff) | (ABS(I(VDUM1))>({isus}))),{1/ron},{1/roff}))  tripdv={tripdv} tripdt={tdt}
RDEL 15 13 10
CDEL 13 0 {cthresh} ; change this for convergence
* Switch control input end
.model DCLAMP D BV={varc}
.ENDS


* Now with SW-switch instead of G-switch
* Here you can choose ron and roff !!
.SUBCKT SPARK_test 1 2 params: vthres=90 varc=10 isus=500m rneg=-1 lpl=130n rpl=2.5k cpar=1p carc=3p
+ trise=10u tfall=10u cthresh=0.01p roff=1e9 ron=1e-1 ioff=100m
.param goff={1/roff} 
.param gon={1/ron} 
.param rparsw=1e12
VDUM1 1 10 0
LPL1 10 11 {lpl} rser=0
RPL1 10 11 {rpl}
CPAR1 1 2 {cpar}
RLEAK1 1 2 {rparsw}
RNEG1 11 17 {rneg}
DTRK1 12 17 DCLAMP
DSRK2 12 16 DCLAMP
CARC1 1 16 {carc}
* G-SWITCH
* G-SWITCH
*G1 16 2 VALUE={v(16,2)*v(13)}  tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
R5 16 2 {rparsw} 
* Changed to SW switch
S1 16 2 13a 0 switch
a1 13 0 0 0 0 0 13a 0 or trise={trise} tfall={tfall}
.model switch SW (vt=0.9 vh=-0.4 ron={ron} roff={roff}) 
* SWITCH END
* Switch control input
*BARC 15 0 v=if(ABS(V(1,2))>{vthres},10,if(ABS(I(VDUM1))>{isus},10,{goff})) tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
*BARC 15 0 v=if((ABS(V(1,2))>{vthres}),10,if(((DDT(ABS(I(VDUM1)))>0 & ABS(I(VDUM1))>ioff) | (ABS(I(VDUM1))>({isus}))),10,goff))  tripdv={tripdv} tripdt={tdt}
BARC 15 0 v=if((ABS(V(1,2))>{vthres}),1,if(((DDT(ABS(I(VDUM1)))>0 & ABS(I(VDUM1))>ioff) | (ABS(I(VDUM1))>({isus}))),1,0))  tripdv={tripdv} tripdt={tdt}
RDEL 15 13 10
CDEL 13 0 {cthresh}
* Switch control input end
.model DCLAMP D BV={varc}
.ENDS

.SUBCKT SWITCH a b c 
s1 a b c 0 sw1
.model sw1 SW (ron=0.01 roff=1e12 vt=1 vh=0)
.ENDS



* input of b4 TABLE is v/us output is a corresponding voltage threshhold factor 
* vthresh2 = vthresh + vthresh*factor 
* if vthresh is higher the sparkgap trip is only at a
* The table values can be taken from the VIgnition/dv/dt curves of a spark-gap data sheet
* The offset produced by the Vthres*V(Ion) product represents the fact that the gas within the spark-gap
* needs a certain amount of time to ionize so that faster transients will reach a higher voltage before the
* gas is ionized and the spark-gap trips. 
* currently the table is filled only till 100V/us but table can be expanded to your needs
* 
.SUBCKT SPARK2 1 2 params: vthres=90 varc=10 isus=500m rneg=-1 lpl=130n rpl=2.5k cpar=1p carc=3p 
+ trise=10u cthresh=10000p tfall=10u fact=1 ron=0.1 roff=1e9 ioff=100m
.param goff={1/roff} 
.param gon={1/ron} 
.param rparsw=1e12
VDUM1 1 10 0
LPL1 10 11 {lpl} rser=0
RPL1 10 11 {rpl}
CPAR1 1 2 {cpar}
RLEAK1 1 2 {rparsw}
RNEG1 11 17 {rneg}
DTRK1 12 17 DCLAMP
DSRK2 12 16 DCLAMP
CARC1 1 16 {carc}
* G-SWITCH
G1 16 2 VALUE={v(16,2)*v(13)}  tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
* Changed to SW switch
*S1 16 2 13a 0 switch
*a1 13 0 0 0 0 0 13a 0 or trise={trise} tfall={tfall}
*.model switch SW (vt=0.9 vh=-0.4 ron=1e-3 roff=1e6) 
R5 16 2 {rparsw} 
* SWITCH END
* Switch control input
*BARC 15 0 v=if(ABS(V(1,2))>v(thresh),10,if(ABS(I(VDUM1))>{isus},10,{goff})) tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
BARC 15 0 v=if((ABS(V(1,2))>v(thresh)),gon,if(((DDT(ABS(I(VDUM1)))>0 & ABS(I(VDUM1))>ioff) | (ABS(I(VDUM1))>({isus}))),gon,{goff}))  tripdv={tripdv} tripdt={tdt}
RDEL 15 13 10
CDEL 13 0 {cthresh} ; added 
* Switch control input end 
E3 thresh 0 VALUE={Vthres+(Vthres*v(ion))} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt} 
b4 ion 0 v=TABLE(v(in)*fact,0,0,1U,.5565M,10M,1M,100M,86M,1,217M,10,521M,100,956M)
E9 in 0 VALUE={abs(V(dvdt))} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
E8 dvdt 0 VALUE={100*v(dif)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
* Diff
E5 x 0 VALUE={V(1,2)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
C4 x dif 1u
R6 dif y 1e6
E6 y 0 VALUE={-100e6*v(dif)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
* Diff end
.model DCLAMP D BV={varc}
.ENDS

* Now with SW-switch instead of G-switch
* Here you can choose ron and roff 
.SUBCKT SPARK2_test 1 2 params: vthres=90 varc=10 isus=500m rneg=-1 lpl=130n rpl=2.5k cpar=1p carc=3p 
+ trise=10u tfall=10u cthresh=0.01p fact=1 roff=1e9 ron=1e-1 ioff=100m 
.param goff={1/roff} 
.param gon={1/ron}
.param rparsw=1e12
VDUM1 1 10 0
LPL1 10 11 {lpl} rser=0
RPL1 10 11 {rpl}
CPAR1 1 2 {cpar}
RLEAK1 1 2 {rparsw}
RNEG1 11 17 {rneg}
DTRK1 12 17 DCLAMP
DSRK2 12 16 DCLAMP
CARC1 1 16 {carc}
* G-SWITCH
*G1 16 2 VALUE={v(16,2)*v(13)}  tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
* Changed to SW switch
S1 16 2 13a 0 switch
a1 13 0 0 0 0 0 13a 0 or trise={trise} tfall={tfall}
.model switch SW (vt=0.5 vh=-0.4 ron={ron} roff={roff}) 
R5 16 2 {rparsw}
* SWITCH END
* Switch control input
*BARC 15 0 v=if(ABS(V(1,2))>v(thresh),10,if(ABS(I(VDUM1))>{isus},10,{goff})) tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
BARC 15 0 v=if((ABS(V(1,2))>v(thresh)),1,if(((DDT(ABS(I(VDUM1)))>0 & ABS(I(VDUM1))>ioff) | (ABS(I(VDUM1))>({isus}))),1,0))  tripdv={tripdv} tripdt={tdt}
RDEL 15 13 10
CDEL 13 0 {cthresh} ; added 
* Switch control input end 
E3 thresh 0 VALUE={Vthres+(Vthres*v(ion))} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt} 
b4 ion 0 v=TABLE(v(in)*fact,0,0,1U,.5565M,10M,1M,100M,86M,1,217M,10,521M,100,956M)
E9 in 0 VALUE={abs(V(dvdt))} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
E8 dvdt 0 VALUE={100*v(dif)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
* Diff
E5 x 0 VALUE={V(1,2)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
C4 x dif 1u
R6 dif y 1e6
E6 y 0 VALUE={-100e6*v(dif)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
* Diff end
.model DCLAMP D BV={varc}
.ENDS


* New Testmodel with digitally controlled switch
* instead of gswitch 
* vthresh = voltage at which the sparkgap start to fire
* varc = arc voltage when sparkgap strikes to his on state
* isus = if sparkgap is on and current is lower isus the spark gap goes to his off state again
* ron = sparkgap on resistance
* roff = sparkgap off resistance
* trise = switching rise time (for soft switching on)
* tfall = switching fall time (for soft switching off - set higher if voltage spike at switchoff occur)
* ioff = should be >10 times the sparkgap off state current = Max. VoltageAtSparkGap/roff but much smaller than isus
*        ( if the sparkgap is off than res1-pin should be zeroed )  
* fact = Since the TABLE voltage source is designed for a 100V sparkgap: some scaling factor
*        for higher spark gap voltages - but of course always change the E4-TABLE source directly if you have your sparkgap data availlable 
  
.SUBCKT SPARK2a_test 1 2 params: vthres=90 varc=10 isus=500m rneg=-1 lpl=130n rpl=2.5k cpar=1p carc=3p 
+ trise=10u tfall=10u fact=1 roff=1e9 ron=1e-1 ioff=100m
.param rparsw=1e12
VDUM1 1 10 0
LPL1 10 11 {lpl} rser=0
RPL1 10 11 {rpl}
CPAR1 1 2 {cpar}
RLEAK1 1 2 {rparsw}
RNEG1 11 17 {rneg}
DTRK1 12 17 DCLAMP
DSRK2 12 16 DCLAMP
CARC1 1 16 {carc}
* G-SWITCH
*G1 16 2 VALUE={v(16,2)*v(13)}  tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
* Changed to SW switch
S1 16 2 13a 0 switch
a1 13 0 0 0 0 0 13a 0 or trise={trise} tfall={tfall}
.model switch SW (vt=0.5 vh=-0.4 ron={ron} roff={roff}) 
R5 16 2 {rparsw}
* SWITCH END
* Switch CONTROL
*** set if voltage at the sparkgap greater than v(thresh) = ON state of sparkgap 
e1 set 0 value={ ABS(V(1,2)) > v(thresh) }
* gives reset only if sparkgap current is much greater than off state current (sparkgap is ON!!) 
* and on state current is actually decreasing AND ... 
* ... AND if on state current goes under isus 
e2 res 0 value={ DDT(ABS(I(VDUM1)))<0 & ABS(I(VDUM1))<isus & ABS(I(VDUM1))>ioff }
A2 set reset 0 0 0 0 13 0 SRFLOP
A3 13 0 0 0 0 0 N015 0 BUF td={2*trise}
A4 0 res 0 N015 0 0 reset 0 AND
* Switch CONTROL end 
E3 thresh 0 VALUE={Vthres+(Vthres*v(ion))} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt} 
b4 ion 0 v=TABLE(v(in)*fact,0,0,1U,.5565M,10M,1M,100M,86M,1,217M,10,521M,100,956M)
E9 in 0 VALUE={abs(V(dvdt))} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
E8 dvdt 0 VALUE={100*v(dif)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
* Diff
E5 x 0 VALUE={V(1,2)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
C4 x dif 1u
R6 dif y 1e6
E6 y 0 VALUE={-100e6*v(dif)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
* Diff end
.model DCLAMP D BV={varc}
.ENDS


.SUBCKT SPARK_90V 1 2 params: vthres=90 varc=10 isus=500m rneg=-1 lpl=130n rpl=2.5k cpar=1p carc=3p 
+ trise=10u tfall=10u cthresh=10p fact=1 roff=1e9 ron=1e-1 ioff=100m
.param goff={1/roff} 
.param gon={1/ron}
.param rparsw=1e12 
VDUM1 1 10 0
LPL1 10 11 {lpl} rser=0
RPL1 10 11 {rpl}
CPAR1 1 2 {cpar}
RLEAK1 1 2 {rparsw}
RNEG1 11 17 {rneg}
DTRK1 12 17 DCLAMP
DSRK2 12 16 DCLAMP
CARC1 1 16 {carc}
* G-SWITCH
G1 16 2 VALUE={v(16,2)*v(13)}  tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
* Changed to SW switch
*S1 16 2 13a 0 switch
*a1 13 0 0 0 0 0 13a 0 or trise={trise} tfall={tfall}
*.model switch SW (vt=0.9 vh=-0.4 ron=1e-3 roff=1e6) 
R5 16 2 {rparsw} 
* SWITCH END
* Switch control input
*BARC 15 0 v=if(ABS(V(1,2))>v(thresh),10,if(ABS(I(VDUM1))>{isus},10,{goff})) tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
BARC 15 0 v=if((ABS(V(1,2))>v(thresh)),gon,if(((DDT(ABS(I(VDUM1)))>0 & ABS(I(VDUM1))>ioff) | (ABS(I(VDUM1))>({isus}))),gon,goff))  tripdv={tripdv} tripdt={tdt}
RDEL 15 13 10
CDEL 13 0 {cthresh}
* Switch control input end 
E3 thresh 0 VALUE={Vthres+(Vthres*v(ion))} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt} 
* Bei schnelleren Wellen spricht der Überspannungsableiter später an !!!
* Bei 20kV statt 200V -> V/100
*b4 ion 0 v=TABLE(v(in),0,0,1U,0.005565M,10M,0.01M,100M,0.86M,1,2.17M,10,5.21M,100,9.56M)
*b4 ion 0 v=TABLE(v(in),0,0,1U,{.5565M*fact},10M,{1M*fact},100M,{86M*fact},1,{217M*fact},10,{521M*fact},100,{956M*fact},1000,{1.5*fact},10000,{2*fact},100000,{2.5*fact},1e6,{3*fact}) tripdv={tripdv} tripdt={tdt}
b4 ion 0 v=TABLE(v(in)*fact,0,0,1U,{.5565M},10M,{1M},100M,{86M},1,{217M},10,{521M},100,{956M},1000,{2},10000,{4},100000,{8},1e6,{16}) tripdv={tripdv} tripdt={tdt}
E9 in 0 VALUE={abs(V(dvdt))} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
E8 dvdt 0 VALUE={100*v(dif)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
* Diff
E5 x 0 VALUE={V(1,2)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
C4 x dif 1u
R6 dif y 1e6
E6 y 0 VALUE={-100e6*v(dif)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
* Diff end
.model DCLAMP D BV={varc} 
.ENDS

.SUBCKT SPARK_90V_test 1 2 params: vthres=90 varc=10 isus=500m rneg=-1 lpl=130n rpl=2.5k cpar=1p carc=3p 
+ trise=1p td=0 tfall=1u cthresh=10p fact=1 roff=1e9 ron=1e-1 ioff=100m
.param goff={1/roff} 
.param gon={1/ron}
.param rparsw=1e12
VDUM1 1 10 0
LPL1 10 11 {lpl} rser=0
RPL1 10 11 {rpl}
CPAR1 1 2 {cpar}
RLEAK1 1 2 {rparsw}
RNEG1 11 17 {rneg}
DTRK1 12 17 DCLAMP
DSRK2 12 16 DCLAMP
CARC1 1 16 {carc}
* G-SWITCH
*G1 16 2 VALUE={v(16,2)*v(13)}  tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
* Changed to SW switch
S1 16 2 13a 0 switch
a1 13 0 0 0 0 0 13a 0 or trise={trise} tfall={tfall} td={td}
.model switch SW (vt=0.5 vh=-0.4 ron={ron} roff={roff}) 
R5 16 2 {rparsw}
* SWITCH END
* Switch control input
BARC 15 0 v=if((ABS(V(1,2))>v(thresh)),1,if(((DDT(ABS(I(VDUM1)))>0 & ABS(I(VDUM1))>ioff) | (ABS(I(VDUM1))>({isus}))),1,0))  tripdv={tripdv} tripdt={tdt}
RDEL 15 13 10
CDEL 13 0 {cthresh}
* Switch control input end 
E3 thresh 0 VALUE={Vthres+(Vthres*v(ion))} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt} 
* Bei schnelleren Wellen spricht der Überspannungsableiter später an !!!
* Bei 20kV statt 200V -> V/100
*b4 ion 0 v=TABLE(v(in),0,0,1U,0.005565M,10M,0.01M,100M,0.86M,1,2.17M,10,5.21M,100,9.56M)
*b4 ion 0 v=TABLE(v(in),0,0,1U,{.5565M*fact},10M,{1M*fact},100M,{86M*fact},1,{217M*fact},10,{521M*fact},100,{956M*fact},1000,{1.5*fact},10000,{2*fact},100000,{2.5*fact},1e6,{3*fact}) tripdv={tripdv} tripdt={tdt}
b4 ion 0 v=TABLE(v(in)*fact,0,0,1U,{.5565M},10M,{1M},100M,{86M},1,{217M},10,{521M},100,{956M},1000,{2},10000,{4},100000,{8},1e6,{16}) tripdv={tripdv} tripdt={tdt}
E9 in 0 VALUE={abs(V(dvdt))} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
E8 dvdt 0 VALUE={100*v(dif)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
* Diff
E5 x 0 VALUE={V(1,2)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
C4 x dif 1u
R6 dif y 1e6
E6 y 0 VALUE={-100e6*v(dif)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
* Diff end
.model DCLAMP D BV={varc} 
.ENDS

* vthres of surge arrester is dependent of volt/us (see table b4)
* set fact parameter to your needs
* or change b4 TABLE directly according to data sheet 
* you can set varc and isus to your needs
.SUBCKT SPARK_400V 1 2 params: vthres={400*1.7} varc=10 isus=10m rneg=-1 lpl=130n rpl=2.5k cpar=1p carc=3p 
+ trise=10u cthresh=10000p fact={100/vthres} ron=0.1 roff=1e9 tfall=10u ioff=100m 
.param goff={1/roff} 
.param gon={1/ron} 
.param rparsw=1e12
VDUM1 1 10 0
LPL1 10 11 {lpl} rser=0
RPL1 10 11 {rpl}
CPAR1 1 2 {cpar}
RLEAK1 1 2 {rparsw}
RNEG1 11 17 {rneg}
DTRK1 12 17 DCLAMP
DSRK2 12 16 DCLAMP
CARC1 1 16 {carc}
* G-SWITCH
G1 16 2 VALUE={v(16,2)*v(13)}  tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
* Changed to SW switch
*S1 16 2 13a 0 switch
*a1 13 0 0 0 0 0 13a 0 or trise={trise} tfall={tfall}
*.model switch SW (vt=0.9 vh=-0.4 ron=1e-3 roff=1e6) 
R5 16 2 {rparsw} 
* SWITCH END
* Switch control input
*BARC 15 0 v=if(ABS(V(1,2))>v(thresh),10,if(ABS(I(VDUM1))>{isus},10,{goff})) tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
BARC 15 0 v=if((ABS(V(1,2))>v(thresh)),gon,if(((DDT(ABS(I(VDUM1)))>0 & ABS(I(VDUM1))>ioff) | (ABS(I(VDUM1))>({isus}))),gon,{goff}))  tripdv={tripdv} tripdt={tdt}
RDEL 15 13 10
CDEL 13 0 {cthresh}
* Switch control input end 
E3 thresh 0 VALUE={Vthres+(Vthres*v(ion))} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt} 
* Bei schnelleren Wellen spricht der Überspannungsableiter später an !!!
* Bei 20kV statt 200V -> V/100
*b4 ion 0 v=TABLE(v(in),0,0,1U,0.005565M,10M,0.01M,100M,0.86M,1,2.17M,10,5.21M,100,9.56M)
*b4 ion 0 v=TABLE(v(in),0,0,1U,{.5565M*fact},10M,{1M*fact},100M,{86M*fact},1,{217M*fact},10,{521M*fact},100,{956M*fact},1000,{1.5*fact},10000,{2*fact},100000,{2.5*fact},1e6,{3*fact}) tripdv={tripdv} tripdt={tdt}
b4 ion 0 v=TABLE(v(in)*fact,0,0,1U,{.5565M},10M,{1M},100M,{86M},1,{217M},10,{521M},100,{956M},1000,{2},10000,{4},100000,{8},1e6,{16}) tripdv={tripdv} tripdt={tdt}
E9 in 0 VALUE={abs(V(dvdt))} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
E8 dvdt 0 VALUE={100*v(dif)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
* Diff
E5 x 0 VALUE={V(1,2)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
C4 x dif 1u
R6 dif y 1e6
E6 y 0 VALUE={-100e6*v(dif)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
* Diff end
.model DCLAMP D BV={varc} 
.ENDS

* vthres of surge arrester is dependent of volt/us (see table b4)
* set fact parameter to your needs
* or change b4 TABLE directly according to data sheet 
* you can set varc and isus to your needs
.SUBCKT SPARK_10kV 1 2 params: vthres={10k*1.7} varc=6000 isus=5 rneg=-1 lpl=130n rpl=2.5k cpar=1p carc=3p 
+ tfall=10u trise=10u cthresh=10000p ron=0.1 roff=1e9 ioff=100m fact={100/vthres}
.param goff={1/roff} 
.param gon={1/ron} 
.param rparsw=1e15
VDUM1 1 10 0
LPL1 10 11 {lpl} rser=0
RPL1 10 11 {rpl}
CPAR1 1 2 {cpar}
RLEAK1 1 2 {rparsw}
RNEG1 11 17 {rneg}
DTRK1 12 17 DCLAMP
DSRK2 12 16 DCLAMP
CARC1 1 16 {carc}
* G-SWITCH
G1 16 2 VALUE={v(16,2)*v(13)}  tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
* Changed to SW switch
*S1 16 2 13a 0 switch
*a1 13 0 0 0 0 0 13a 0 or trise={trise} tfall={tfall}
*.model switch SW (vt=0.9 vh=-0.4 ron=1e-3 roff=1e6) 
R5 16 2 {rparsw} 
* SWITCH END
* Switch control input
*BARC 15 0 v=if(ABS(V(1,2))>v(thresh),10,if(ABS(I(VDUM1))>{isus},10,{goff})) tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
BARC 15 0 v=if((ABS(V(1,2))>v(thresh)),gon,if(((DDT(ABS(I(VDUM1)))>0 & ABS(I(VDUM1))>ioff) | (ABS(I(VDUM1))>({isus}))),gon,{goff}))  tripdv={tripdv} tripdt={tdt}
RDEL 15 13 10
CDEL 13 0 {cthresh}
* Switch control input end 
E3 thresh 0 VALUE={Vthres+(Vthres*v(ion))} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt} 
* Bei schnelleren Wellen spricht der Überspannungsableiter später an !!!
* Bei 20kV statt 200V -> V/100
*b4 ion 0 v=TABLE(v(in),0,0,1U,0.005565M,10M,0.01M,100M,0.86M,1,2.17M,10,5.21M,100,9.56M)
*b4 ion 0 v=TABLE(v(in),0,0,1U,{.5565M*fact},10M,{1M*fact},100M,{86M*fact},1,{217M*fact},10,{521M*fact},100,{956M*fact},1000,{1.5*fact},10000,{2*fact},100000,{2.5*fact},1e6,{3*fact}) tripdv={tripdv} tripdt={tdt}
b4 ion 0 v=TABLE(v(in)*fact,0,0,1U,{.5565M},10M,{1M},100M,{86M},1,{217M},10,{521M},100,{956M},1000,{2},10000,{4},100000,{8},1e6,{16}) tripdv={tripdv} tripdt={tdt}
E9 in 0 VALUE={abs(V(dvdt))} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
E8 dvdt 0 VALUE={100*v(dif)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
* Diff
E5 x 0 VALUE={V(1,2)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
C4 x dif 1u
R6 dif y 1e6
E6 y 0 VALUE={-100e6*v(dif)} tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
* Diff end
.model DCLAMP D BV={varc} 
.ENDS

* Limited integrator with reset 
.subckt SDTx in out reset  
+PARAMS: min=-1e10 max=1e10 Ci=10m ron=1e-6 roff=1e6 
G1 0 out VALUE={if(time>0,V(in)*Ci*(((V(in)>0 & V(out)<max))|((V(in)<0)&(V(out)>min))),0)} tripdv=1 tripdt=1
S1 out 0 reset 0 SW1 
C1 out 0 {Ci}
.model SW1 VSWITCH (Ron={Ron} Roff={Roff} Von=0.9 Voff=0.1)
.ends

.subckt risefall in out params: trise=100m tfall=100m 
Erise inx 0 VALUE={  IF(   v(in)>0.5&v(out)<=1,  1/trise,   IF  (v(in)<0.5&v(out)>=0,  -1/tfall  ,0 ))   }  tripdv=1 tripdt=1
Xint inx out reset SDTx params: min=0 max=1
Rout out 0 1e6
Rreset reset 0 1e6
.ends

