* Another model at the ltspice Yahoo group
* Voltage dependent resistor (varistor)

* External node designations
* Node 1 -> A terminal
* Node 2 -> B terminal
* VBO is the turn-on threshold at
* which the device conducts 1mA.
*************************************************

* if Vr smaller 0.71 1ma before VBO, exponent should be higher
* if Vr higher 0.71 1ma after VBO, exponent should be smaller
* if Vr=0.71 1ma at VBO
.SUBCKT mov 1 2 ; base generic
+PARAMS: VBO=10 Vr=0.71 exp=20
.param Vratio={VBO/Vr} 
B1 1 2 I=if(V(1, 2)-0.5, (V(1, 2) / Vratio) ** exp, (1 / Vratio) ** exp) tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
B2 2 1 I=if(V(2, 1)-0.5, (V(2, 1) / Vratio) ** exp, (1 / Vratio) ** exp) tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
.ENDS

.SUBCKT mov_400V 1 2 ;2xVN/1.73205
+PARAMS: VBO=461V Vr=1.2 exp=17
.param Vratio={VBO/Vr} 
B1 1 2 I=if(V(1, 2)-0.5, (V(1, 2) / Vratio) ** exp, (1 / Vratio) ** exp) tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
B2 2 1 I=if(V(2, 1)-0.5, (V(2, 1) / Vratio) ** exp, (1 / Vratio) ** exp) tripdv={tdv} tripdt={tdt}
.ENDS

